<Profile title="AI-assisted business operations | Dave Bettner" page="work" description="AI-assisted product direction, creative delivery, and supplier-development workflows.">
  <article class="section wrap business-case">
    <h1>Building the workflows behind a business</h1>
    <p class="lead">I used AI tools to build an operating application and delivery workflows for a small creative-services and commerce portfolio.</p>
    <p>My work connected client intake, creative review, template delivery, and supplier qualification, turning owner requests into software and decision packets.</p>
    <article>
      <h2>An operating home for client work</h2>
      <p>I directed AI-assisted development of an application for client context, intake, content schedules, and creative review. The onboarding workflow brings the client brief, working plan, sample assets, and owner feedback into one review path.</p>
      <p>The owner can review context and proposed work together before deciding what moves forward.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Templates recipients can use</h2>
      <p>I led preparation of reusable template kits and checked the recipient workflow in the native design tool: make a copy, edit text, replace a photo, and export at full size.</p>
      <p>The handoff includes editable masters and recipient-copy links so the owner can customize a kit and prepare it for delivery.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Supplier research tied to the product brief</h2>
      <p>I translated product and fulfillment requirements into supplier comparisons, qualification criteria, and an owner-review packet. The comparison connects materials, packaging, minimum orders, samples, fulfillment terms, and open questions in one decision packet.</p>
      <p>This gives the owner a concrete basis for choosing the next supplier question or sample request.</p>
    </article>
    <details>
      <summary>Implementation details</summary>
      <p>The application includes implemented onboarding and simulated role previews. Template checks cover specific versions and recipient workflows. Supplier work covers research and qualification preparation; physical sample acceptance and launch are later steps.</p>
    </details>
    <h2>Try the workflow</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/showcase/creative-operations-lab/">creative-operations lab</a> is a synthetic browser demo with invented records and no live integrations. Change the concept revision to see how approval and supplier evidence need to follow the current version.</p>
    <h2>The role I want next</h2>
    <p>I’m looking for my next role building AI tools and agent workflows, bringing accounting judgment, enterprise implementation, and practical business operations.</p>
    <p><a href="/work/">Selected work</a></p>
  </article>
</Profile>
